 write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:10:05-07:00","id":1401682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401666-first-vtmv-clanbook?p=1401673#post1401673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't think those will sell. And they would be mostly retreading the same ground anyway. Those supplements were mostly fluff. You can't fill an entire clanbook with just rules and metaplot updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:17:00-07:00","id":1401685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401666-first-vtmv-clanbook?p=1401682#post1401682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't think those will sell. And they would be mostly retreading the same ground anyway. Those supplements were mostly fluff. You can't fill an entire clanbook with just rules and metaplot updates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah though there are some clans that where changed greatly in comparison to V20 like Tremere that are now 4 clans or Hecata that is iirc 4 clans into one.<br /> First you can describe how the situation is for those four house and second you can describe how it is exactly comming and how it is working that those clans work now as one together.<br /> <br /> And what is wrong with filling it with fluff? The Anarch book is mainly fluff too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T07:26:58-07:00","id":1401688,"title":"","content":"No, the Anarch book was mostly fiction. There's nothing wrong with fluff, retreading the same fluff though is obsolete. It is claimed that V5 is not a reboot, so except for metaplot and mechanics you're still dealing with much of the same lore. Could you go so deep into these recent changes that it would fill an entire book per clan? Sure, but apparently the developers don't believe that would sell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T09:51:15-07:00","id":1401703,"title":"","content":"1. I also remember them mentioning that they do not want new clan books. I can not say where.<br /> 2. For most Clans I still feel on firm ground in V5 relying on older material.<br /> 3. For some Clans (Tremere and Hecata in particular) I feel a need a new book <i>ist needed</i>. They have <i>changed so radically</i> that the old stuff is out the window and the new material is very thin.<br /> <br /> Maybe Cults is an example of how you can do a Clan in half a book? I have not read it yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","user":"mfalkenb","date":". 07-08-2020, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T10:29:20-07:00","id":1401706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401666-first-vtmv-clanbook?p=1401703#post1401703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Cults is an example of how you can do a Clan in half a book? I have not read it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they did a good job of it, and could see them doing something similar with the Tremere and a Blood Sorcery book. Maybe even combine with ThinBlood Alchemy and Resonances and cover the potentiality of the blood.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T10:31:08-07:00","id":1401707,"title":"","content":"Overall, individual clan books have gone the way of the dodo. If we get something like that again it would be another lore of the clans as the issue is that a Clan Book sells only to a small section of the playerbase and even then.By compiling all of the clans into one book, you are going to reach the largest amount of players in one swing with a little less detail but it makes it much more of a viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T10:32:15-07:00","id":1401708,"title":"","content":"I do not have Cults either and it would be a shame if there is no clan book. I am a new player like many other people and for the new it would be very helpful to have a book better explaining the clan. Of course you could say that you could just go back to older material but for some clans it is not really helpful and for the rest it is kind of poor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:03:55-07:00","id":1401742,"title":"","content":"How is it poor? The revised edition run of clanbooks are excellent material that still holds up amazingly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:12:49-07:00","id":1401760,"title":"","content":"That you need to go to old OoP Material. Mayby for english speaker this is no issue with everything getting only PoD even the old books but for the translations like German your only chance would be getting second hand books of more or less two decades long ago edition. Then those books are with an gehenna incomming and a working masquerade. New people like myself that are only buying what is in there language will get disappointed with it. If you think this is not an issue well it whas shown very good with D&amp;D where D&amp;D 4 whas non existent in the DACHL Region because of no translations and D&amp;D 5 became only a hit after it whas translated. If Paradox would really want with VTMV to get all those new players that only heard from VTM like a myth or because they played Bloodlines than they should get those peoples actual Clanbooks too.<br /> <br /> But yeah mayby the point of view is just to different with the european market wanting things translated and getting books printed and bound professionally from big publishers while the US is happy with PoD and mostly PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:16:43-07:00","id":1401800,"title":"","content":"I am European myself. But from a language area too small to ever get translations of any RPG books. So our roleplay culture has always predominantly been based on English language products. It's what we are used to. I think the same is true for much of the continent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:49:39-07:00","id":1401805,"title":"","content":"I'd love some updated clan-specific merits. If they won't do clanbooks, they should at least do Lore of the Clans composite books so we can get that sort of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T17:54:19-07:00","id":1401814,"title":"","content":"I understand the &quot;no more clanbooks&quot; strategy is floating around out there.<br /> <br /> I wonder, though...<br /> <br /> A new vtm video game is coming at... some point? If it is (fingers crossed) a huge hit, and if there is popular support for it among the gaming community, and given the business model of licensing parts of the line out to other publishers, could that policy change? It's hard to imagine somebody walking away from a potentially profitable product, even if the overall profit is low.<br /> <br /> In any case, as to the original question of the first clan to get a book? I'd bet on thinbloods, if that counts as a clan. Brand new mechanics. Brand new fluff. Seriously, these folks are nothing like the old thinbloods or caitiff. They need a book, if only to explain and expand alchemy.<br /> <br /> Among actual clans, as mentioned above, Hecata and Tremere are likely in need of a new book. The Lasombra, Banu Haqim, and the Ministry have seen some <i>big</i> changes since their last book, too. All five deserve a book.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Tzimisce and Ravnos. Umm, yeah, you know the deal.<br /> <br /> So, eight-ish badly needed books.<br /> <br /> For that matter, as much as they claim it is the same setting some of the mechanical changes to clan flaws, and how they relate to fluff and setting, could use some exploration. Like how:<ul><li>Brujah become more frenzy-prone as they age, while earlier fluff implied the opposite. How do they deal with calm neonates and hair-trigger elders?</li> <li>Gangrel can now count on their animal features fading after exactly one night. Plus, the &quot;leave us alone we're busy surviving&quot; clan is avowedly anarch.</li> <li>Malkavians seem to have changed their mind on Dominate/Dementation yet again. Plus, it's impossible to learn Dementation without Obfuscate. What's up with all that?</li> <li>Nosferatu start out pug-ugly, but find it harder to hide their vampirism as time goes on. What about their looks actually changes?</li> <li>Toreador are less supernaturally powerful outside of beautiful places. How has this impacted classic starving artist/gutter glam concepts?</li> <li>Ventrue (especially the young) can now break their feeding limitation with relative ease. Oh, and I doubt <i>everyone</i> misses Hardestadt.</li> </ul><br /> Bottom line:<br /> I'm ready to give the publishers money in exchange for clan-related mechanics and setting updates. Please, let me give you money for clanbooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T21:44:24-07:00","id":1401853,"title":"","content":"You can consider the Player Guide of Modiphius as the proximus Lore of the Clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T22:31:12-07:00","id":1401857,"title":"","content":"I would buy a clanbook just to have some clan specific merits, like maybe something allowing me to use Earthmeld without a rouse-check. Just a nifty little quality of life merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T14:35:46-07:00","id":1401970,"title":"","content":"Prior devs have stated that the previous clanbooks didn't sell well for what they were. I'd lay zero money on them going back to that model.<br /> <br /> The current WW devs also stated that the design methodology was to have things come up where their stories can be expanded upon along with other things, in the detail needed. So I would forsee less clan compendium books and more utility books with a clan in them. Not that we have much clan material left to go, beyond the weird outlier 'we exist because of our Discipline!' bloodlines. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401666-first-vtmv-clanbook?p=1401853#post1401853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can consider the Player Guide of Modiphius as the proximus Lore of the Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. We were told that the writeups of the clans in the PG would bei nt he vein of the core book, so sevenish pages plus powers on average in comparison. Unless WW has severely changed how they're planning on doing it, which could have happened. But I doubt it. The PG is meant to work in addition to the core book and other books, not replace those books (so you'll get Lasombra with the same metaplot timing as the Chicago book, but it won't be in full chapters detail like the Chicago book)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401666-first-vtmv-clanbook?p=1401857#post1401857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would buy a clanbook just to have some clan specific merits, like maybe something allowing me to use Earthmeld without a rouse-check. Just a nifty little quality of life merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more likely what we'll see in the Player's Guide, assuming it ever appears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 07-09-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}